insert into public.lessons (topic_id, objectives, explanation, code_lang, code, code_explanation, activity, mistakes, recap, version) select id, '["Explain performance optimization in your own words.","Recognise and apply: optimise images (right size, modern format) before adding more code.","Recognise and apply: lazy-load below-the-fold content and split large bundles.","Complete the practical activity and check it against the success criteria."]'::jsonb, '["This lesson covers performance optimization: measuring and improving load time: images, code splitting and caching. It is written for a complete beginner, so every idea is introduced in plain language before any code appears.","The first key idea is that optimise images (right size, modern format) before adding more code. In practice that means a learner should be able to recognise it in a real page or project, not only repeat a definition. Work through the example below slowly and predict what each line does before reading its explanation.","The second key idea is that lazy-load below-the-fold content and split large bundles. This is the idea most beginners get wrong, so the common-mistakes section below shows the wrong version next to the corrected version.","Finally, remember that how performance optimization fits into real web development work. A professional developer does not memorise every detail — they understand the idea, practise it on a small real task, and check their work. That is exactly what the practical activity at the end of this lesson asks you to do."]'::jsonb, 'javascript', '// Next.js Image optimises automatically:
