insert into public.lessons (topic_id, objectives, explanation, code_lang, code, code_explanation, activity, mistakes, recap, version) select id, '["Explain deployment with vercel in your own words.","Recognise and apply: connect the GitHub repo so every push deploys; set env vars in the dashboard.","Recognise and apply: a production deploy must be opened and tested, not just marked ''ready''.","Complete the practical activity and check it against the success criteria."]'::jsonb, '["This lesson covers deployment with vercel: deploying a Next.js app to Vercel with env vars and preview/production. It is written for a complete beginner, so every idea is introduced in plain language before any code appears.","The first key idea is that connect the GitHub repo so every push deploys; set env vars in the dashboard. In practice that means a learner should be able to recognise it in a real page or project, not only repeat a definition. Work through the example below slowly and predict what each line does before reading its explanation.","The second key idea is that a production deploy must be opened and tested, not just marked ''ready''. This is the idea most beginners get wrong, so the common-mistakes section below shows the wrong version next to the corrected version.","Finally, remember that how deployment with vercel fits into real web development work. A professional developer does not memorise every detail — they understand the idea, practise it on a small real task, and check their work. That is exactly what the practical activity at the end of this lesson asks you to do."]'::jsonb, 'bash', '# Vercel dashboard: Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables
