insert into public.lessons (topic_id, objectives, explanation, code_lang, code, code_explanation, activity, mistakes, recap, version) select id, '["Explain production project architecture in your own words.","Recognise and apply: separate routes, components, data access and server actions into clear layers.","Recognise and apply: log errors without secrets; fail closed on auth and payment checks.","Complete the practical activity and check it against the success criteria."]'::jsonb, '["This lesson covers production project architecture: structuring a production app: layers, boundaries, logging and safe failure. It is written for a complete beginner, so every idea is introduced in plain language before any code appears.","The first key idea is that separate routes, components, data access and server actions into clear layers. In practice that means a learner should be able to recognise it in a real page or project, not only repeat a definition. Work through the example below slowly and predict what each line does before reading its explanation.","The second key idea is that log errors without secrets; fail closed on auth and payment checks. This is the idea most beginners get wrong, so the common-mistakes section below shows the wrong version next to the corrected version.","Finally, remember that how production project architecture fits into real web development work. A professional developer does not memorise every detail — they understand the idea, practise it on a small real task, and check their work. That is exactly what the practical activity at the end of this lesson asks you to do."]'::jsonb, 'typescript', '// Layer order: route -> server action/API -> Supabase (RLS) -> Postgres.
